WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.175 --> 00:00:18.197
Jack groaned when his alarm went off the next morning.

2
00:00:22.379 --> 00:00:26.461
"Yay!" Luke shouted from his own bed.

3
00:00:26.481 --> 00:00:29.123
"I get to watch swim practice today!"

4
00:00:29.143 --> 00:00:33.009
"Great," Jack muttered sarcastically.

5
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:38.473
His mother planned to stay at his practice today to make sure he didn't ditch it again.

6
00:00:39.554 --> 00:00:41.295
That meant Luke was staying too.

7
00:00:42.636 --> 00:00:44.277
Jack hauled himself out of bed.

8
00:00:44.837 --> 00:00:45.698
His back hurt.

9
00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:53.963
Yesterday, after his parents lectured him for approximately five million hours, they'd made him clean the kitchen and

10
00:00:54.063 --> 00:00:55.364
sweep and mop the floor.

11
00:00:56.425 --> 00:01:00.548
The only good thing about living in a small apartment was that it didn't take too long to

12
00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:00.988
clean it.

13
00:01:02.728 --> 00:01:05.531
Jack's parents had also made him email his coach.

14
00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:12.679
He apologized for quitting the team and politely asked—begged, really—for another chance.

15
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.064
Hours later Coach Shin sent a short response: "See you tomorrow."

16
00:01:18.985 --> 00:01:24.010
As Jack put on his swimsuit and brushed his teeth, he wondered if Coach Shin would lecture him

17
00:01:24.211 --> 00:01:25.392
and give him chores too.

18
00:01:28.716 --> 00:01:32.679
He pictured himself scrubbing the deck of the pool while his teammates laughed at him.

19
00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:36.983
"I hate it here," he said to his reflection in the mirror.

20
00:01:37.003 --> 00:01:38.965
"Why did we ever move?"

21
00:01:39.946 --> 00:01:41.006
Jack went to the kitchen.

22
00:01:44.009 --> 00:01:48.773
His dad was standing by the stove, dressed for work in a button-down shirt and khaki pants.

23
00:01:49.814 --> 00:01:55.458
He lifted a ham-and-cheese omelet from a pan on the stove, slid it onto a plate, and passed

24
00:01:55.498 --> 00:01:56.339
it to Jack's mother.

25
00:01:58.696 --> 00:02:02.219
She put a buttery toasted bagel on the plate and handed it to Jack.

26
00:02:02.239 --> 00:02:05.802
"Enjoy," she said brightly.

27
00:02:06.863 --> 00:02:07.383
"Thank you.

28
00:02:07.984 --> 00:02:10.866
I'm really sorry about skipping practices," he said.

29
00:02:10.886 --> 00:02:17.271
"You apologized last night, and we've forgiven you," his mother said, sitting next to him at the small

30
00:02:17.311 --> 00:02:17.952
kitchen table.

31
00:02:17.972 --> 00:02:23.476
"I know it's hard to be the new guy in town," Jack's father said.

32
00:02:23.496 --> 00:02:27.620
"My first day of work here, I showed up in a business suit and tie.

33
00:02:28.288 --> 00:02:31.309
I was completely overdressed and completely embarrassed."

34
00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:34.431
"It's hard to be the new girl in town too.

35
00:02:35.171 --> 00:02:40.293
I miss my friends in Oklahoma and my book club and my walking group," Jack's mother said.

36
00:02:40.313 --> 00:02:43.114
"It's going to take time to get adjusted."

37
00:02:44.695 --> 00:02:45.355
Jack nodded.

38
00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:48.837
"I miss Noah and the other kids on the swim team.

39
00:02:49.717 --> 00:02:52.618
And, honestly, I miss being the best swimmer on the team.

40
00:02:53.699 --> 00:02:56.060
It seems like some of the kids here are really fast."

41
00:02:57.004 --> 00:03:01.286
"Competing with fast swimmers will help you improve your speed," Jack's father said.

42
00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:05.568
"But it's still hard," his mother said sympathetically.

43
00:03:05.588 --> 00:03:07.989
"Yeah," Jack said.

44
00:03:08.009 --> 00:03:09.470
"It's really hard."

45
00:03:10.631 --> 00:03:14.292
A few minutes later, Jack headed to the car with his mother and Luke.

46
00:03:17.614 --> 00:03:18.974
Laura was waiting there for them.

47
00:03:19.995 --> 00:03:21.916
Jack said hello but that was all.

48
00:03:22.752 --> 00:03:27.813
He spent most of the car ride staring silently out the window while Laura chatted politely with his

49
00:03:27.853 --> 00:03:35.236
mother. When they got to the community pool, Coach Shin nodded at him.

50
00:03:35.676 --> 00:03:39.377
"Hello, Jack," he said, his tone more stern than welcoming.

51
00:03:40.297 --> 00:03:42.838
"Thank you for letting me come back," Jack mumbled.

52
00:03:44.078 --> 00:03:45.478
One of his teammates sneered.

53
00:03:45.498 --> 00:03:46.799
"What are you doing here?

54
00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.499
I thought you quit the team."

55
00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:50.620
Jack didn't answer.

56
00:03:51.456 --> 00:03:54.538
The team did drills for the first 15 minutes of practice.

57
00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.302
Jack struggled hard but was able to keep up.

58
00:04:01.223 --> 00:04:04.705
And this time he didn't accidentally hum any Long-Hair Boys songs.

59
00:04:04.725 --> 00:04:08.367
"We've got only a few days before the meet.

60
00:04:08.808 --> 00:04:11.389
Let's make these practices count," Coach Shin said.

61
00:04:11.409 --> 00:04:14.812
"Last year the Pacific Piranhas beat us by two points.

62
00:04:15.532 --> 00:04:17.313
I don't want that to happen again.

63
00:04:18.554 --> 00:04:20.375
We'll start with the breaststroke today.

64
00:04:20.756 --> 00:04:23.198
Line up and swim across the pool and back.

65
00:04:23.918 --> 00:04:27.061
Pretend you're competing in the meet, and give it your best."

66
00:04:28.081 --> 00:04:29.563
Hulk was first in line.

67
00:04:30.363 --> 00:04:32.685
He practically flew across the pool.

68
00:04:36.148 --> 00:04:38.670
It wasn't just his huge size that made him fast.

69
00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:47.097
His streamline, a technique for swimming underwater, was perfectly straight, and he wasted no breaths and no motions.

70
00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:51.060
Watching him, Jack felt awed and envious.

71
00:04:52.808 --> 00:04:54.870
"He's incredible," Jack thought.

72
00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:58.092
"Definitely the best swimmer I've ever seen."

73
00:04:59.473 --> 00:05:04.616
When Jack's turn came, he swam as hard as he could and got a great time, close to

74
00:05:04.656 --> 00:05:05.597
his personal best.

75
00:05:09.179 --> 00:05:10.440
He knew he couldn't beat Hulk.

76
00:05:11.201 --> 00:05:13.582
But he thought he'd swum faster than most of the kids.

77
00:05:14.623 --> 00:05:22.764
As Jack emerged from the water, his brother clapped and shouted, "Yay, Jack!

78
00:05:23.025 --> 00:05:24.185
You're the bestest!"

79
00:05:24.205 --> 00:05:26.727
"Aww!" a girl said.

80
00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:30.049
"That little boy adores his big brother."

81
00:05:31.049 --> 00:05:32.090
"So sweet!"

82
00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:33.431
another girl said.

83
00:05:34.591 --> 00:05:36.352
Then Jack heard Laura's voice.

84
00:05:37.153 --> 00:05:39.094
"Luke is such a cutie," she said.

85
00:05:39.114 --> 00:05:41.195
"Luke and Jack look a lot alike."

86
00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:45.398
"Whoa!" Jack thought as he stared at Laura.

87
00:05:46.318 --> 00:05:47.939
"I think she just called me a cutie!"

88
00:05:48.599 --> 00:05:49.340
Jack grinned.

89
00:05:50.108 --> 00:05:53.071
Maybe it wasn't so bad having Luke come to his practices!

90
00:05:53.091 --> 00:05:56.033
"Come here, Jack," Coach Shin ordered.

91
00:05:56.854 --> 00:06:00.077
Uh-oh. Jack hunched his shoulders and walked over to the coach.

92
00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:05.281
Coach Shin put his hand on Jack's shoulder.

93
00:06:05.301 --> 00:06:09.185
"You swam the breaststroke much better today than last week.

94
00:06:09.765 --> 00:06:11.207
But you need to work on your form.

95
00:06:11.607 --> 00:06:13.829
You're not cupping your hands enough when they hit the water."

96
00:06:13.849 --> 00:06:15.230
"All right.

97
00:06:15.631 --> 00:06:17.072
Thank you," Jack said.

98
00:06:17.832 --> 00:06:19.053
Strangely, Mrs.

99
00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:20.815
Wilson had told him the same thing.

100
00:06:21.455 --> 00:06:23.697
Well, she'd actually shouted it at him.

101
00:06:24.698 --> 00:06:29.181
Jack returned to the water and tried following Coach Shin's advice—and Mrs.

102
00:06:29.241 --> 00:06:33.004
Wilson's. Cupping his hands more did seem to help a little.

103
00:06:34.606 --> 00:06:39.069
Jack and his teammates spent the next hour or so working on all the swim strokes.

104
00:06:42.552 --> 00:06:47.860
By the end of practice, Jack had done very well on the freestyle, okay on the backstroke, and

105
00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:52.201
pretty badly on the butterfly—but the "fly" stroke had always been hard for him.

106
00:06:53.282 --> 00:06:56.462
A few of the guys said, "Nice job" or "Not bad."

107
00:06:57.583 --> 00:07:00.423
At the end of practice, Jack approached Coach Shin.

108
00:07:03.764 --> 00:07:05.465
Nervously he cleared his throat.

109
00:07:06.945 --> 00:07:10.746
"Coach, I want to apologize again for skipping practices.

110
00:07:11.546 --> 00:07:12.767
Thank you for letting me come back."

111
00:07:12.787 --> 00:07:15.748
"Apology accepted and you're welcome.

112
00:07:16.388 --> 00:07:17.148
I'm glad you're back."

113
00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:24.265
The coach's tone wasn't exactly warm—more like lukewarm—but that was good enough for Jack.

114
00:07:24.285 --> 00:07:30.350
"It looks like your strengths are the breaststroke and the freestyle," Coach Shin said.

115
00:07:31.551 --> 00:07:32.151
Jack nodded.

116
00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:35.093
"I hope I can help our team beat the Pacific Piranhas."

117
00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:36.975
The coach shook his head.

118
00:07:37.495 --> 00:07:38.196
"I have a rule.

119
00:07:38.756 --> 00:07:43.160
Anyone who misses more than one practice isn't allowed to compete at the next meet."

120
00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:48.184
"But—" "That's my rule," Coach Shin said abruptly.

121
00:07:48.824 --> 00:07:51.645
"You follow it, or quit the team for real this time."

122
00:07:52.765 --> 00:07:53.686
Jack hung his head.

123
00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:56.066
"I understand," he mumbled.

124
00:07:56.947 --> 00:07:58.947
He did understand, sort of.

125
00:07:59.828 --> 00:08:02.689
But somehow it still felt incredibly unfair.
